Package: remotedesktop-client
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCHITECTURE@
Maintainer: Remote Desktop <noreply@example.invalid>
Homepage: https://github.com/gaozeqian/RemoteDesktop
Depends: libx11-6, libxext6, libxi6, libxrandr2, libxcursor1, libxfixes3, libxrender1, libxcb1, libfontconfig1, libfreetype6, libgl1, libpulse0, libavcodec62, libavutil60, libswscale9
Description: Remote Desktop client (controls another computer)
 Shows another computer's screen in a window and sends this machine's keyboard
 and pointer to it.
 .
 The window is the whole of it: this package has no service and runs nothing in
 the background. Installing it does not make this machine reachable — that is
 the separate `remotedesktop-host` package — so it is safe to install on a
 machine that is only ever the one doing the controlling.
 .
 The libraries above are loaded by name when the window is first drawn rather
 than at startup, so without them the program would start and then fail to show
 anything. They are the toolkit's, not this program's: X11 and OpenGL for the
 window, PulseAudio for the sound coming back from the other machine, and
 libavcodec for decoding its screen.
